    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires the `Owner` GET response to include an `initials` field \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes, following the existing `displayName` pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field (and it's serialized in the GET response).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `initials` computing `Character.toUpperCase(firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\"`.\n\nThe target test `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` passes (`\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`) and the full suite builds green.",
